# Pairs with AckedOccupies. Both layers that keep an acknowledged write in its
# offset fail together: the post-failure resync re-seeds beneath an abandoned
# call still in motion (issue #5799), and the store does not refuse that call
# landing at an occupied offset. The reissued write is acknowledged, then the
# abandoned call lands over it. Either layer alone keeps AckedOccupies: the
# store's create-only rows are what kept #5799's run from losing a write.
MODULE: AckedOccupiesRewindWithoutCreateOnly
TARGET: AckedOccupies
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the resync re-seeds beneath an abandoned call and the store lets it land over the reissue
PERTURBS: Resync, LateLand

--- FIND
    /\ resyncing = "resync"
    /\ inflight = {}
    /\ next' = ReseedNext
--- REPLACE
    /\ resyncing = "resync"
    /\ inflight = {}
\* MUTATION: re-seed from the store alone.
    /\ next' = RecoveredNext
--- END

--- FIND
               /\ ~WithCrossSiloMove \/ curFresh
               /\ occ[o] = "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no create-only refusal; the late call lands over an occupant.
               /\ ~WithCrossSiloMove \/ curFresh
--- END
